' 09 PathMap delivery: a send on p, a receive on q, and the second send of a peek.
'
' Source of Figure 1 in ../pathmap-prefix-delivery.md. The figure restates the
' delivery plans of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/pathmap/delivery.rs,
' the markers of spaces/pathmap/markers.rs and the path rules of
' spaces/outer/pathmap.rs, as the engine model of PathMapPrefix.v and the
' model PathMapPrefix.tla state them. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. Every operation checks its path first: at most 64 elements, and no
'      PathMap or zipper inside an element.
'   2. A send on p offers its datum x to PRODUCE-WAITERS(p): the waiters of
'      I(p), I(parent(p)), ..., I(eps), the most specific prefix first. The
'      first waiter that binds the re-rooted datum and whose guard admits it
'      fires. A refusal moves on (decision 37).
'   3. A fire is one COMM on I(q) with the vehicle of x, which is never
'      stored. A waiter that does not peek spends a non-persistent x.
'   4. A send that no waiter spends stores x on D(p) and one marker on each
'      index channel I(q), q a prefix of p, in depth order.
'   5. A receive on q takes the first datum of CONSUME-CANDIDATES(q) that its
'      pattern binds. It checks the guard once, and a refusal parks it.
'   6. The COMM on I(q) consumes the marker of the datum on q. A persistent
'      datum stays, and a persistent receive then re-issues (a divergent
'      pair). A delivery that does not peek retires the record and the other
'      markers with single-channel K_retire COMMs.
'   7. A peek of a non-persistent datum sends it again (decision 45, Rule E).
'      A fire of a waiter that does not peek spends it. With no such fire,
'      the marker of the COMM is stored again with its identity. At the fire
'      cap, FINISH stores the marker again before the commit, and the settle
'      job carries the offer of the datum (open item O-2).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 09-pathmap-delivery.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 09-pathmap-delivery
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title PathMap delivery (P5e): a send on p, a receive on q, and the second send of a peek

start
if (the path has more than 64 elements,\nor an element holds a PathMap or a zipper?) then (yes)
  :PathTooDeep or UnsupportedPathElement,
  before any staging; <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (the operation?) then (send x on p)
  :PRODUCE-WAITERS(p): the waiters of I(p), I(parent(p)), …, I(ε),
  the most specific prefix first, each prefix in its discipline order; <<$rrs_agent>>
  while (a later waiter W on a prefix q binds R(p∖q, x)\nand its guard admits x? (a refusal moves on)) is (yes)
    :one COMM on I(q): the vehicle of x
    (the marker pars and the payload) meets W.
    The vehicle is never stored; <<$rrs_effect>>
    if (x is not persistent and W does not peek?) then (yes)
      :x is spent: a fresh send never stored it; <<$rrs_effect>>
      stop
    else (no)
      if (W is persistent?) then (yes)
        :re-issue the send: the next round
        offers x to W again; <<$rrs_reject>>
        stop
      else (no)
        :x stays in flight
        (W peeks, or x is persistent); <<$rrs_flow>>
      endif
    endif
  endwhile (no)
  :STORE-MARKERS: store x on D(p), then the marker
  of x on each I(q), q ⪯ p, in depth order (ε first); <<$rrs_storage>>
else (receive K on q)
  :d ← the first datum of CONSUME-CANDIDATES(q)
  (path keys in byte order, the exact path first)
  whose re-rooted payload the pattern of K binds; <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (a datum d was found and the guard of K admits it?\n(the guard is checked once)) then (no)
    :park K on I(q); <<$rrs_storage>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :one COMM on I(q) over the marker m_q(d),
  with R(p∖q, payload(d)) bound; <<$rrs_effect>>
  if (d is persistent?) then (yes)
    :d and all of its markers stay; <<$rrs_storage>>
    if (K is persistent?) then (yes)
      :re-issue K: a divergent pair; <<$rrs_reject>>
    else (no)
    endif
  else (no)
    if (K peeks?) then (yes)
      :the COMM removed m_q(d) only.
      The second send of d (decision 45, Rule E)
      has the identity and the cost authority of d; <<$rrs_flow>>
      if (the transaction made FIRE_ROUND_CAP fires?) then (yes)
        :FINISH stores m_q(d) again before the commit (O-2).
        The settle job carries the offer of d, and the offer
        of a d that another job spent stores nothing; <<$rrs_storage>>
      else (no)
        :PRODUCE-WAITERS(p), the most specific prefix first; <<$rrs_agent>>
        if (a waiter that does not peek fires on d?) then (yes)
          :RETIRE-PLAN: K_retire of D(p):r and of every
          other marker of d, one channel each; <<$rrs_fail>>
        else (no)
          :store m_q(d) again with its identity:
          d is stored as before the peek; <<$rrs_storage>>
        endif
      endif
    else (no)
      :RETIRE-PLAN: K_retire of D(p):r, then of the marker
      of d on each prefix other than q, one channel each; <<$rrs_fail>>
      if (K is persistent?) then (yes)
        :K takes the next candidate in the next round; <<$rrs_agent>>
      else (no)
      endif
    endif
  endif
endif
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_agent>    | a choice of the plan: an order of the prefixes, the candidates or the waiters |
|<$rrs_effect>   | a COMM that the plan stages |
|<$rrs_flow>     | a datum in flight, or the second send of a peek (Rule E) |
|<$rrs_fail>     | a retire: K_retire COMMs on single channels |
|<$rrs_storage>  | a stored record, a restored marker or a parked waiter |
|<$rrs_reject>   | a failure or a re-issue, with no staging of the operation |
endlegend
@enduml
